{
  "id": "u12-l04",
  "unit": "u12-have-to",
  "title": "I can",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**পারা 'can' takes the ordinary present endings:**\n\n- আমি **পারি** · তুই **পারিস** · তুমি **পারো** · সে **পারে** · আপনি **পারেন**\n\nThe person stays **আমি, তুমি, সে** here, not the -কে form: **আমি গাড়ি চালাতে পারি** 'I can drive', but **আমাকে গাড়ি চালাতে হবে** 'I have to drive'.\n\n'Can't' = **পারি না**, with না at the very end: **আমি লিখতে পারি না** 'I can't write'.\n\n**বুঝতে পারি** 'I can understand' is the usual way to say you understand a language: **আমি বাংলা বুঝতে পারি**.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "paro",
      "bn": "পারো",
      "tr": "paro",
      "en": "you (familiar) can"
    },
    {
      "id": "parish",
      "bn": "পারিস",
      "tr": "parish",
      "en": "you (intimate) can"
    },
    {
      "id": "likhte",
      "bn": "লিখতে",
      "tr": "likhte",
      "en": "to write",
      "notes": "Infinitive of লেখা; the stem is লিখ- as in লিখি."
    },
    {
      "id": "chalate",
      "bn": "চালাতে",
      "tr": "chalate",
      "en": "to drive",
      "notes": "Infinitive of চালানো. গাড়ি চালাতে পারি \"I can drive\"."
    },
    {
      "id": "bujhte",
      "bn": "বুঝতে",
      "tr": "bujhte",
      "en": "to understand",
      "notes": "Infinitive of বোঝা. বুঝতে পারি \"I can understand\"; বুঝতে পারছি না \"I don't understand (right now)\"."
    }
  ],
